  "notes": "Surface derived 2026-07-26 from the merged FedID Digital Credentials draft: the static userAgentAllowsProtocol() method (unknown protocol \u2192 false, never throws; ReferenceError when DigitalCredential is undefined \u2014 typeof guard required), the required protocol member across DigitalCredentialGetRequest/CreateRequest and the echoed DigitalCredential.protocol attribute, and the two protocol enumerations (presentation: openid4vp-v1-unsigned/-signed/-multisigned, org-iso-mdoc; issuance: openid4vci-v1). The deprecation of unspecified protocols (Chrome 151 developer trial behind DigitalCredentialsProtocolFilter, removal targeted for Chrome 160) is documented as listing-vs-detail separated facts; BCD rows (141/26/mirror) are kept apart from the 151/160 timeline. Substantive MDN check: API/DigitalCredential and the userAgentAllowsProtocol_static subpage both 404 (Case B). Deliberately partial pending independent review."
